Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its specialized agents, is pleased to submit a comprehensive proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in the City of Belval. Our solution leverages cutting-edge technologies, including large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), to provide intelligent assistance across various administrative activities. We are committed to meeting the City's requirements for efficiency, quality, security, and sustainability while ensuring compliance with all regulatory frameworks.

### 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an AI solution that assists municipal agents in their daily tasks, enhancing access to information, improving response quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must integrate with existing systems, ensure data sovereignty, protect sensitive information in accordance with GDPR, and minimize environmental impact. Our consortium has carefully reviewed the tender requirements, ensuring our proposal addresses all aspects, including functional scope, regulatory compliance, security constraints, technical performance, budgetary limitations, and sustainability goals.

### 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution is built around a sovereign LLM model, Mistral 7B Instruct, which will be self-hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure provided by OVHcloud or Outscale to ensure compliance with EU regulations and data sovereignty requirements. The TechnicalArchitect Agent has designed an architecture that utilizes Docker and Kubernetes for efficient deployment and management, ensuring scalability and security. To meet the performance requirement of < 2 seconds response time, we will implement auto-scaling, caching, and other optimization techniques as necessary.

For API integration with existing systems such as civil status, town planning software, EDM, and user directories, we will leverage our experience with REST, GraphQL, and SOAP APIs. The AIInnovation Agent proposes a RAG system for accurate information retrieval, fine-tuning of the LLM on a domain-specific corpus to adapt to municipal agent needs, and implementation of explainability methods to ensure transparency.

The SecurityCompliance Agent ensures that our solution adheres to strict security controls, including GDPR compliance, with tools for anonymization like Microsoft Presidio and custom NER models. We enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) and role-based access control (RBAC), utilizing privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

The Budget Agent confirms our financial eligibility to bid, with an average 3-year revenue meeting the minimum turnover threshold and sufficient bonding capacity. Our projected margin for the project is approximately 840,000 euros, assuming a target gross margin percentage of 28% on the total contract value of 3 million euros over 4 years.

The CSRSustainability Agent highlights our commitment to reducing energetic consumption through partnerships with green hosting providers like OVHcloud and Scaleway, who use 100% renewable energy. Our digital sobriety practices include model quantisation, auto-scaling, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy, aiming to reduce energy consumption by around 35%.

The Legal Agent has reviewed the tender requirements, ensuring our compliance with GDPR, particularly Article 6(1)(e), and our policy of no automated decision without human validation. We are prepared to provide a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) template version 3.2 and support DPIA as needed.

### 4. Unaddressed Requirements
After careful review of the tender document and our agents' contributions, we have addressed all specified requirements. However, we note that the exact costs for certain components, such as the detailed breakdown of exploitation costs over the four-year period, will require further analysis in the project's planning phase to ensure optimal cost management while maintaining the quality of service expected by the City of Belval.

### 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., with its consortium of specialized agents, is confident in our ability to deliver a comprehensive AI solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for efficiency, quality, security, and sustainability. Our proposal integrates cutting-edge technologies with a deep understanding of regulatory compliance, security constraints, and environmental considerations. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and explore how we can contribute to the digital transformation of the City's administrative services.
